  - autoGranularity: a span of exactly 4 or 10 years falls into the shorter bucket. Years are 365.25 days. Identical timestamps give month, but if they are all 1 January 00:00 UTC they give year. The month rule checks only the day of the month, so the time of day is ignored. The year rule requires 00:00 UTC, as the spec says.
  - bucketRange throws on non-finite min or max.

  Caveats for the caller:
  - ISO codes win over meaning. A literal "NA" in a country column becomes Namibia and "No" becomes Norway. Filter out n/a-style tokens first if the column can contain them.
  - timeColumnScore follows the spec's substring rule, so "Sentiment" (contains "time") and "Candidate" or "Updated" (contain "date") score 0.6. timeRecognitionRate filters them out, because their values do not parse as dates.
